40,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The financial data is quite sobering. We are paying for empty space at a significant monthly cost, and every single desk move incurs a specific fee. We cannot afford a trial-and-error approach to this layout.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that some parts of the room are much noisier than others, especially near the printer. Also, the physio said it takes a long time to get our chairs and desks just right for our bodies.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,May,,"Wow, the data is eye-opening! It takes up to nine minutes just to get screens working every morning. Plus, with our arrival times being so spread out, any ""first-come"" system is totally unfair to the late arrivals!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems we're all discovering that our ""ideal"" plan is a myth. The survey shows a blatant disregard for daylight, and our history of shuffles proves that we're terrible at predicting our own needs. We're just guessing.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I found that sitting close together really helps... The project strands last spring stopped needing written notes because they could just ask each other. Even the new joiners learned a lot just by overhearing us.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, while the social benefits of proximity are clear, we must balance them against the financial reality. If we prioritize ""closeness"" without a precise plan, we risk wasting budget on costly revisions.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I understand the budget is important, but I'm worried about the chairs. If it takes days to make a spot feel right for our bodies, moving too often might make us feel tired or sore.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, you're so right! If we're already spending nearly ten minutes just plugging things in, adding physical discomfort to the mix is a nightmare. We need a plan that doesn't eat up our precious time or energy!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you're focusing on the minutes, but the real nightmare is the silence. We have a survey full of people complaining about the lack of light, yet the plan just ignores it. We're pretending every seat is equal when they clearly aren't.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Um, I think... if we ignore the social side, we might save money, but we'll lose that natural way of helping each other. I'm worried that if we're too far apart, we'll stop talking.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, I value the team's cohesion, but we must be honest about our constraints. We are paying for space we aren't using, and every change costs us. We need a layout that is final and fiscally responsible.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I agree that we should be careful with the budget. But if we pick a spot that's too noisy or doesn't fit us, we might feel sad or tired. Can we make sure comfort is written in the plan?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,May,,"@Victoria, being ""final"" is great, but not if it means we're stuck with a routine that drains us! If we're wasting ten minutes every morning just to start working, that's a hidden cost that's way worse than a one-time fee.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, ""fiscally responsible"" is a convenient shield. The real cost is the resentment building up because some people get the window and others get the wall. If we don't address the inequality of the seats now, we're just planning for another shuffle.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I understand the budget and the light are important. But I'm just worried that if we only focus on the costs, we'll forget that who we sit next to really matters for how we feel.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"It is clear we are all prioritizing different risks—financial, physical, and social. However, we must acknowledge that without a stable budget, none of these goals are sustainable. We need a solution that minimizes repeated costs and maximizes our current space.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I hope we can find a way to balance everything. If we can pick spots that are quiet and comfortable for our bodies, and stay there, maybe we can save money and be happy too!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,May,,"@Victoria, I get the budget thing, but let's not forget the human cost! If we're all stressed and wasting time every morning, productivity drops. We need a layout that's efficient for our actual lives, not just the ledger!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, your focus on the ledger is predictable, but it's a distraction. The real issue is that we're pretending this is a collective decision while ignoring that some of us will end up in the dark. Let's stop the pretense.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't want anyone to feel resentful or alone. If we can just find a way to be close enough to help each other, maybe the other problems won't feel so overwhelming. I hope we can do that.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
