64,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Looking at the options, Option C is completely untenable. Given the nine-minute setup time May mentioned and the physical calibration Minato noted, a free-address system would be a daily drain on productivity and health.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I agree with Victoria. If we have to change our chairs and screens every single day, it would be so tiring! I think we would all feel very sore and sad if we couldn't keep our spots cozy.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,May,,"@Victoria, @Minato, you're speaking my language! Option C is a total disaster. Imagine wasting nearly ten minutes every single morning just to start working? That's a nightmare for my schedule! I'm voting against it.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option C is a joke. It doesn't just waste time; it rewards the early birds with the window seats while the rest of us fight for the scraps. It's the ultimate way to avoid admitting that some seats are worse than others.,"{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. Option C sounds very stressful. If we don't have a place to call our own, I think it would be even harder to start talking to people. I don't think I'd feel comfortable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, you are correct that seat quality varies. However, Option B is a financial disaster. Rotating the entire team would incur repeated facilities charges for re-running power and network, which our stagnant budget simply cannot sustain.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I agree that moving all the time sounds expensive. But I'm also worried that if we shift blocks, we'd have to spend days fixing our chairs and desks over and over again. That doesn't sound very peaceful.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, @Minato, you've convinced me! Option B is just a slower version of the Option C nightmare. Why would we want to reset our whole lives every few months? It's a waste of time and energy!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, you're finally focusing on the right thing—the cost of movement. But let's be honest: Option B is just a facade of fairness. It rotates the misery of the wall seats without ever actually deciding who deserves them. It's a coward's compromise.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Option B would be confusing. If we keep moving, I'm worried we won't be able to build a real connection with the people around us. It feels like we'd just be starting over again and again.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"Option A is the only rational choice. It eliminates the repeated costs of Option B and the daily inefficiency of Option C. By assigning seats permanently, we ensure financial stability and physical consistency for everyone.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I think Option A is the best! If we have our own spots, we can take our time to make them perfectly cozy and quiet. It sounds like the most peaceful way for everyone to work.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,May,,I'm totally on board with Option A! It's the only way to protect our time and energy. No more morning chaos or constant resets—just a stable spot where we can actually get to work! I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A is the only logical choice, but let's stop pretending it's a magic fix. It solves the budget and the setup time, but it leaves us with the window problem. We need to decide who takes the wall seats now, not later. I vote A.","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. Option A seems the safest. If we have a permanent spot, I think it'll be easier for me to feel comfortable and actually talk to the people next to me. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree with the consensus. Option A is the only choice that respects our financial constraints and prevents unnecessary waste. I vote for Option A to ensure a stable and sustainable environment for the team.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm so happy we all agree! I'll vote for Option A too. Let's just make sure we all help each other find the quietest and most comfortable spots so everyone feels happy! I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,May,,It's a wrap! Option A is the only one that doesn't treat our mornings like a race or a chore. Let's keep our time and our sanity! I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Since we've reached a consensus, I'll cast my vote. But let's be clear: the ""stability"" of Option A only works if we're honest about the seat disparity. I vote for Option A, provided we actually decide who sits in the dark.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm glad we could all agree. I hope that by having a fixed spot, we can really focus on supporting each other and building a team where no one feels left out. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
